{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>There is an evil.</b> רב in the language of the Holy Scriptures has four meanings. The first: רב that is the opposite of מעט, as in 'תרבו את נחלתו' (you shall increase his inheritance). The second: רב את יוצרו, from the root ריב. The third: רב in the sense of 'רבה רשת,' but it is of the doubled [forms], like 'השמיעו על בבל רבים,' and the alef after it indicates this, and it is on the pattern of 'דלים רכים,' and it is a past-tense verb from רכים, as in 'כי רך לבבך'; likewise 'וברקים רב,' and the vav at the beginning of the verse indicates it, as in 'וישלח חציו ויפיצם.' The fourth: great, as in 'מושיע ורב,' and 'והצילם על כל רב ביתו,' 'קרית מלך רב,' and it is David, in the same sense as 'קרית חנה דוד.' Some interpret it as the place, but it is not correct, because it does not account for the phrase 'המלות ותהיינה למלך הרב.' The masculine plural form is 'רבי המלך,' and the feminine form is 'רבה,' and 'רבה' here is upon the man."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The comment cites numerous biblical phrases in highly abbreviated form without verse references; each has been left as Ibn Ezra presents it. The phrase 'רבה רשת' is textually uncertain and rendered hyper-literally. The argument about grammatical forms and patterns is compressed and obscure in the original; preserved as such."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:56.182622052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}